1
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:19,100
What happened?

2
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:21,271
The baby-sitter called.

3
00:00:21,271 --> 00:00:23,500
His daughter is sick.

4
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:25,226
What's wrong?

5
00:00:25,226 --> 00:00:29,300
I think she has a stomachache.

6
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:33,600
He's a good father.

7
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,500
So... what do you think of him?

8
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:39,700
He's very nice.

9
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:42,314
But I think he was nervous tonight.

10
00:00:42,314 --> 00:00:47,796
It was his first date in two years.

11
00:00:47,796 --> 00:00:49,400
Will you see him again?

12
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:54,000
I hope so.

13
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,600
This food is delicious.

14
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:59,800
He didn't get a thing to eat.

15
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,100
You ordered enough for three or four people,

16
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:04,404
but I'm not complaining.

17
00:01:04,404 --> 00:01:07,966
The food is delicious.

18
00:01:07,966 --> 00:01:09,600
Who is that?

19
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:11,300
Do you think it's...

20
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:19,400
No. You won't believe it, Marilyn!

21
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:25,000
I believe it. Even without looking.

22
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:25,783
Hi!

23
00:01:25,783 --> 00:01:26,400
How...?

24
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:29,900
Your downstairs neighbor let me in.

25
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:30,612
Did you go home?

26
00:01:30,612 --> 00:01:31,700
I did , but everything is OK,

27
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:34,600
so I decided to come back.

28
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:36,700
To apologize for leaving so early,

29
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,200
I brought you a little gift.

30
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:39,900
It's a bonsai tree

31
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:42,200
for your new apartment.

32
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:44,000
Hi, Marilyn. I hope it's not too late.

33
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,700
Oh, not at all. We're still eating.

34
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:49,543
Please, come in. Join us.

35
00:01:49,543 --> 00:01:53,000
It's our meal from the restaurant.

36
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,900
And how is your daughter?

37
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:55,300
Oh, she's fine.

38
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:57,626
It was only a tummy ache.

39
00:01:57,626 --> 00:01:59,652
It's good that you went back.

40
00:01:59,652 --> 00:02:02,900
Yes, I think it's important for me to be there

41
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:04,500
since her mother died.

42
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:09,300
I agree. Aren't you hungry?

43
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:12,300
As a matter of fact... I am hungry.

44
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:15,500
There's lots of food left.

45
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:17,800
Mmm, this is delicious!

46
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,600
Enjoy!

47
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:21,300
I'm going to excuse myself.

48
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:25,236
I have a lot of work to do to get ready for tomorrow.

49
00:02:25,236 --> 00:02:26,906
Good night, Harry. It was nice meeting you.

50
00:02:26,906 --> 00:02:28,500
Bye, Marilyn.

51
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:29,500
Good night, Susan.

52
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:32,600
Good night, Marilyn.

53
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:35,400
She's going to a fashion show here in the city tomorrow.

54
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:36,938
She is sleeping here

55
00:02:36,938 --> 00:02:39,500
so she won't have to travel from Riverdale in the morning.

56
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:42,000
You two must be close.

57
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,543
we are.

58
00:02:43,543 --> 00:02:47,100
The whole Stewart family is close.

59
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:57,200
I like that.

60
00:02:57,200 --> 00:03:01,300
And then, two years ago, my wife died.

61
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:03,626
You miss her.

62
00:03:03,626 --> 00:03:06,700
I do...yes, but I have Michelle...

63
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:10,900
and with time...

64
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:14,200
Is there anyone else in your life?

65
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:19,100
No, not yet. What about you?

66
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:21,600
Oh, I date occasionally,

67
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:23,600
but my work keeps me busy.

68
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:25,850
Ooh, speaking of keeping busy-

69
00:03:25,850 --> 00:03:27,300
I have an early start tomorrow,

70
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:30,660
and the baby-sitter has to get home.

71
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:32,417
Where did the time go?

72
00:03:32,417 --> 00:03:38,090
It's midnight.

73
00:03:38,090 --> 00:03:39,242
Thank you, Susan.

74
00:03:39,242 --> 00:03:41,900
I had a nice evening.

75
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:50,830
Me, too, Harry.

76
00:03:50,830 --> 00:03:52,500
Harry?

77
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:53,900
Yes?

78
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:57,800
I'd like to meet your daughter someday.

79
00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:00,100
Does that mean that I can see you again?

80
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:01,300
Of course.

81
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:03,200
Wonderful. I'll call you,

82
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:04,400
and we'll go out to dinner.

83
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:04,600
Please do.

84
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:06,700
I promise I won't leave early.

85
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:09,800
It was for a good reason.

86
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:12,300
You know something?

87
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:12,600
What?

88
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:16,414
I think we're going to be good friends.

89
00:04:16,414 --> 00:04:17,500
Good night, Susan.

90
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:19,300
Good night, Harry,

91
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:28,800
Have a safe trip home.

92
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:31,400
Are you all right?

93
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:33,200
Sorry.

94
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:37,800
I never liked that umbrella stand.

95
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:40,800
Good night, Harry.
